---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /tajima-convoy/
pageKey: convoy
locationId: convoy
title: "Tajima Ramen Convoy | The Original, on Convoy Street Since 2001"
description: "Tajima Ramen Convoy, the original, on Convoy Street since 2001. Communal tables, the full menu plus an expanded izakaya list, and okonomiyaki. Walk in, no reservations."
---
{#
  /tajima-convoy/. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md, plus the shared location page
  template above it.

  The highest-traffic page on the site: 9,704 clicks, 678,630 impressions. It
  owns `best ramen san diego` (130 clicks), not the home page. It is also doing
  the worst work of the six on the money keyword, ARP 5.47 / SoLV 26.5%, because
  it sits in the densest ramen market in San Diego. The brief: "Content quality
  matters more here than anywhere."

  MUST NOT READ AS A NEAR-DUPLICATE OF MERCURY. They are in the same ZIP and
  Google is already mis-resolving the two entities (localstack lists Convoy at
  Mercury's address, frankiapp puts Convoy in Los Angeles). Everything below is
  specific to this room.

  THE "TWO MILES" FIGURE IS WRONG AND IS GONE, 2026-09-09. SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md
  states it in three places and this page published it as a section heading.
  Connor's GBP coordinates put the two rooms 0.57 miles apart in a straight
  line. The number is removed and not replaced with a computed one: see
  _convoyMercuryDistance in _data/roomPlaces.json. The strategic point is
  unaffected and if anything sharper, because two rooms that close are more
  likely to be conflated, not less.

  NAP comes from locations.json, hours included: confirmed 2026-09-09.
#}
{%- set spriteIcons = ["ramen-bowl"] %}
{% include "components/icon-sprite.njk" %}

{%- set loc = (locations.items | where("id", locationId)) | first %}

<section class="page-hero page-hero--split" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="page-hero__inner">
    <div>
      <p class="page-hero__crumbs">
        <a href="/">{{ site.name }}</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <a href="/locations/">Locations</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span class="page-hero__crumbs-current">{{ loc.name }}</span>
      </p>
      <h1 class="page-hero__title" id="page-title">{{ loc.name }}</h1>
      {#
        REWRITTEN ENDING. The concept closed with "it still sets the standard
        for the other five." voice-tone.md: "Every sentence is a fact. No
        sentence tells the reader what to think about the facts." Replaced with
        the fact that carries the same weight without grading the other rooms.
      #}
      <p class="page-hero__lede">
        The room Sam Morikizono took over in 2001, on the street San Diego goes to for ramen. It was already called Tajima. It is still the room the rest of the house grew out of.
      </p>

      {#
        The address plate. Every value from locations.json, none hardcoded.
        The Hours row is components/plate-hours.njk, shared with the other two
        location templates so the three cannot drift again.
      #}
      <address class="plate">
        <span class="plate__item">
          <span class="plate__label">Address</span>
          <span class="plate__value">{{ loc.address.street }}, {{ loc.address.locality }}, {{ loc.address.region }} {{ loc.address.postalCode }}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="plate__item">
          <span class="plate__label">Phone</span>
          <a class="plate__value" href="{{ loc.phone | telHref }}">{{ loc.phone }}</a>
        </span>
        {% include "components/plate-hours.njk" %}

        <span class="plate__item">
          <span class="plate__label">Directions</span>
          <a class="plate__value" href="{{ loc | mapsUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open in Maps<span class="u-visually-hidden">, opens in a new tab</span></a>
        </span>
        <span class="plate__item">
          <span class="plate__label">Parking</span>
          <span class="plate__value">{{ loc.parking }}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="plate__item">
          <span class="plate__label">Seating</span>
          <span class="plate__value">Walk in. No reservations.</span>
        </span>
        <span class="plate__item">
          <span class="plate__label">Happy Hour</span>
          <a class="plate__value" href="/happy-hour/">See times</a>
        </span>
        {#
          REPOINTED 2026-08-05. This sent people to /order-online/, which then
          asked them to pick the location they were already reading about.
          Straight to Convoy's own Toast page now, from locations.json.
        #}
        <span class="plate__item">
          <span class="plate__label">Order</span>
          <a class="plate__value" href="{{ loc.orderUrl }}" rel="noopener">Order online</a>
        </span>
      </address>
    </div>

    {#
      THE WORDPRESS HOTLINK IS GONE, 2026-09-10, AND THAT CLOSES A LAUNCH
      BLOCKER. This <figure> loaded its photograph from tajimaramen.com, the
      live site this project replaces, which meant the highest-traffic page on
      the build could not survive the old site being taken down, in either
      order. It was the last remote image outside our own origin.

      What replaces it is a real photograph of this room, supplied by the
      client at review and committed to public/images/photo/. It is
      machine-upscaled and flagged `aiUpscaled` in photos.json with the whole
      story. It is not AI-generated imagery and it is not a placeholder;
      DESIGN_SYSTEM.md draws that distinction under Banned content. Replace it
      when the documentary shoot lands.

      It comes through roomPhotos.js like every other placed photograph, so it
      passes the same build guards, including the one that fails the build on
      unreviewed alt.

      The alt and caption said "storefront" until the v2 port. The photograph
      is the dining room, and it shows the communal table this page goes on to
      describe.
    #}
    {%- set convoyHero = roomPhotos[locationId].hero %}
    <figure class="page-hero__photo">
      <img class="page-hero__photo-img"
        src="{{ convoyHero.src }}"
        alt="{{ convoyHero.alt }}"
        loading="lazy" width="{{ convoyHero.width }}" height="{{ convoyHero.height }}">
      <figcaption class="page-hero__photo-cap">{{ convoyHero.caption }}</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "components/location-place.njk" %}

{# ==================== WHAT'S DIFFERENT HERE ==================== #}
{#
  Brief: "the one section that must not be templated." Everything here is
  specific to Convoy and none of it is true of Mercury.
#}
<section class="sect pattern-section" aria-labelledby="diff-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="diff-title">Where the house <em>started.</em></h2>
    </header>

    <div class="diff">

      <article class="cell diff__cell diff__cell--wide reveal">
        <h3 class="diff__title">The <em>original.</em></h3>
        <p class="diff__body">
          In 2001, Sam took over a small Japanese restaurant on Convoy Street. The name was already on the door. Convoy is San Diego's Pan-Asian district, and this room has held its corner of it for twenty-five years. Read the whole story on <a class="sect__link" href="/about/">the About page</a>.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="cell diff__cell reveal">
        <h3 class="diff__title">Communal tables.</h3>
        <p class="diff__body">
          Long shared tables, the way the room has always run. You sit with the neighborhood.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="cell diff__cell reveal">
        <h3 class="diff__title">The full menu, plus izakaya.</h3>
        <p class="diff__body">
          Every bowl, plus an expanded izakaya list you will not find at the ramen-bar locations. <a class="sect__link" href="/menu/">See the menu</a>.
        </p>
      </article>

      {#
        Okonomiyaki stays. The brief is explicit: "Keep okonomiyaki on the page.
        It earns 56 clicks and it is a real quirk of this room."

        SOFTENED. The concept read "in the room run by a chef from just outside
        Osaka." Sam being from Amagasaki, near Osaka, is confirmed. Him running
        this kitchen day to day in 2026 is not, and the sentence implies it.
        The Osaka connection is stated without putting anyone at the pass.

        FLAG: okonomiyaki is not in menu.json, because it is not in the
        CLIENT_FACTS.md dish list. It belongs in the Toast pull.
      #}
      <article class="cell diff__cell reveal">
        <h3 class="diff__title">Okonomiyaki.</h3>
        <p class="diff__body">
          A Convoy quirk. The savory Osaka-style pancake, in a house founded by someone who grew up just outside Osaka.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="cell diff__cell reveal">
        {# From locations.json, not written out. College Heights already did it
           this way; Convoy was the copy that could drift. #}
        <h3 class="diff__title">{{ loc.languages | length }} languages.</h3>
        <p class="diff__body">
          {{ loc.languages | join(", ") }} spoken at this location.
        </p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ==================== FROM THIS KITCHEN ==================== #}
{#
  REWRITTEN note. The concept read "Tonkotsu simmered twelve hours." No simmer
  time is confirmed anywhere in CLIENT_FACTS.md.

  The bowls shown are filtered from menu.json, so this gallery cannot drift
  from the menu page or from schema.

  READS AS A MENU, 2026-09-09. Each figure carries the dish description under
  the name now, from the same menu.json field /menu/ prints. Convoy keeps its
  photographs rather than taking the type-only list the other six use
  (components/location-menu.njk), because Convoy is the one room with its own
  food photography and every featured dish here is photographed. Printing the
  same eleven names again as a list underneath would repeat the section, not
  deepen it.

  No prices. menu.json `_priceStatus`: the brand prices are stale against the
  live catalogs and vary by location, so no single price is right for all
  seven. /menu/ prints them; a location page does not.

  NOW FILTERED BY LOCATION. This looped every featured dish with an image,
  which happened to equal Convoy's eleven, so the page was right by
  coincidence rather than by rule. The other two templates already filtered on
  `dish.locations`.
#}
<section class="sect sect--alt sect--rule" aria-labelledby="kitchen-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <span class="mark mark--lg mark--disc sect__mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#i-ramen-bowl"></use></svg></span>
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="kitchen-title">What comes out of <em>Convoy.</em></h2>
      <p class="sect__note">
        The Red, Black, and White trio, and an izakaya list that runs deeper here than anywhere else in the house. <a class="sect__link" href="/menu/">See the whole menu</a>.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="bento">
      {%- for dish in menu.items %}
        {%- if dish.feature and dish.image and locationId in dish.locations %}
      <figure class="cell shot reveal">
        {#- See components/location-gallery.njk: without .shot__figure the
            absolutely positioned image covers its own caption. #}
        <div class="shot__figure">
          <img class="shot__img" src="{{ dish.image }}" alt="{{ dish.alt }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ dish.imageWidth }}" height="{{ dish.imageHeight }}">
        </div>
        <figcaption class="shot__caption">
          <span class="shot__name">{{ dish.name }}</span>
          {%- if dish.description %}<span class="shot__desc">{{ dish.description }}</span>{% endif %}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
        {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
      {#-
        The twelfth cell. menu.json yields eleven photographs at Convoy and the
        bento is four columns, so the last row was one short. This fills it
        with a Convoy izakaya plate that is not on the brand menu, which is
        what the section note above actually promises. Curated in
        roomPhotos.js, so it goes through the same build guard as every other
        placed photograph. -#}
      {%- set extra = roomPhotos[locationId].dishes %}
      {%- if extra %}
      {%- for shot in extra %}
      <figure class="cell shot reveal">
        <div class="shot__figure">
          <img class="shot__img" src="{{ shot.src }}" alt="{{ shot.alt }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ shot.width }}" height="{{ shot.height }}">
        </div>
        <figcaption class="shot__caption">
          <span class="shot__name">{{ shot.caption }}</span>
          {%- if shot.tag %}<span class="shot__tag">{{ shot.tag }}</span>{% endif %}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- endif %}
    </div>

    {#- Convoy does not render components/location-menu.njk (it shows its own
        food photography instead of the type list), so it includes the menu
        links directly. -#}
    {%- set menuLinksLoc = locationId %}
    {% include "components/menu-links.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

